      },
      "message": "feat(ui): camcraft-ui builds and links for wasm32 (#31 rung 2)\n\nCut the native-only seams out of the shared UI so camcraft-ui.wasm links\nfor wasm32-unknown-unknown next to rung 1's camcraft-cli.wasm:\n\n- egui_app/shell.rs split: the winit loop, window, surface and GPU\n  bring-up move to egui_app/shell_window.rs, the per-frame draw and the\n  ApplicationHandler to shell_window/frame.rs. They (plus gpu_init,\n  frame_watch, os_quit) are native-only. shell.rs keeps the shared frame\n  (shell_layout, dock tabs, viewport panel, headless proof). On wasm32\n  egui_app::run refuses the windowed entry by name (exit 2).\n- file_dialog: one FileDialog seam for the 13 rfd sites; native forwards\n  to rfd unchanged, wasm32 answers None (cancelled) with a diagnostic.\n  egui-winit and rfd become native-only dependencies.\n- camcraft_app::clock::Instant: std's Instant natively, web_time's on\n  wasm32 (std's panics there). web-time 1.1 was already in the lock.\n  geometry's projection profiler reads the clock only when profiling.\n- web/build-app-wasm.sh also builds and links camcraft-ui.wasm.\n\nThe browser runner, async GPU bring-up, async file picker, thread\nfallbacks and the wasi JS shim are still owed.\n\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
